### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018A&A...617A.120M: Simple chemical model cannot explain inner DCO+ 5-4 emission; single physical profile adopted
- 2017ApJ...835..174S: Missing flux on scales >4.6'' (1.5 kpc)
- 2017ApJ...835..174S: Only four CO transitions constrain few free parameters; two-phase relies on assumptions
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Inner 50 AU cannot be modeled due to low resolution and dust optical depth
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Matched-filter fluxes are only lower limits
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Parameterized models include no chemistry; formation route cannot be distinguished
- 2013Sci...341..630Q: Vertical disk structure is uncertain; vertical N2H+ boundaries fixed
- 2018A&A...612L..11S: Single-dish data cannot constrain the complex outflow; the CSE model is crude
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Data did not initially pass QA2 due to low elevation and array configuration
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Uniform sphere geometry is a clear limitation; masses are first-order
- 2015A&A...581A..85P: Resolution too low to fully resolve the disk; edge-on view unfavourable
- 2015A&A...581A..85P: Mass loss rate is a lower limit and uncertain by factor ~3; SO data cannot constrain density and temperature
- 2019MNRAS.486.2366M: Temperature, velocity gradient and density poorly constrained and correlated
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Coarse spectral resolution (3.4 km/s) may overestimate dispersions and Mach number; Mach number is an upper bound
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Cloud line-of-sight extent unknown; PPV not equivalent to physical space
- 2025A&A...696A..31G: Gas temperatures poorly constrained by HCNH+; large-scale emission filtered; beam dilution neglected
- 2020ApJ...889...43Z: Wall temperature >=100 K cannot be confirmed by the data
- 2020ApJ...889...43Z: Resolution insufficient for firm disk conclusion in SMA2
- 2015ApJ...806...17R: Warm-gas mass per nucleus uses global Herschel ratio
- 2020MNRAS.498L..87B: Emission unresolved; cannot distinguish envelope from disk; S hot corino needs higher resolution
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Errors underestimated; isothermal assumption fails in center; SO2 fits unsatisfactory
- 2020A&A...644A..59K: Beam filling factors set to 1; no collisions with e- and H
- 2021A&A...645A..45C: Strong parameter degeneracies in LVG models
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2024ApJ...969..143I: Cosmic ray ionization estimate uncertain by order of magnitude; N(H2CO) poorly constrained
- 2015ApJ...814..143A: Smooth spherical shell model does not reproduce fine structure; infrared pumping only partly included
- 2020MNRAS.493.3744F: FIR SED poorly sampled so L_IR and SFR are lower limits; kinematics unresolved; SLED has too few points
- 2014ApJ...795...28B: Mass-loss rate is poorly constrained; density is an upper bound, column a lower bound, layer thickness unknown
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Did not recover high temperatures (>100 K) at the cloud edge; limited angular resolution and sensitivity
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Uncertainties exclude systematics from fixed parameters
- 2020A&A...643A..89P: Inner outflow fluxes uncertain due to broad nuclear profile; CO(4–3) excess unexplained
- 2025ApJ...986L..22R: Two-component model is a simplification of the dual-jet geometry; March 17 S/N lower
- 2024ApJ...972..147C: LVG parameters highly degenerate; large uncertainty in non-thermal index; unknown CI excitation
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Radial extent unresolved; beam dilution underestimates column densities
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Continuum oversubtraction/blocking may reduce line flux
- 2014ApJ...785..149S: Single-component modelling of a heterogeneous sample; no single model fits (chi2 min 10.4 for 3 dof); degeneracies remain; differential magnification not accounted
- 2019ApJ...870L..26C: Ad-hoc use of phase calibrator scans for sky subtraction leaves standing waves and sky lines and high noise
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: gamma Vir models lack constraints at other wavelengths; temperature minimum cannot be analyzed
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: Variability at longer timescales cannot be ruled out for gamma Lep
- 2025A&A...696A.100G: Exact chemical pathways and relative contributions of bottom-up and top-down processes remain unquantified; models omit PAH chemistry
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Peak brightness cannot be converted to density without non-LTE excitation modelling, which needs more than one line.
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Models are non-rotating and omit chemistry, so SASI signatures cannot be assessed.
- 2020ApJ...889L...4L: HI column densities are lower limits for most sightlines (optically thin assumption)
- 2015MNRAS.447.3936M: Detailed chemical modelling beyond scope; T_k assumed uniform; vibrational/electronic states neglected
- 2017MNRAS.469.3347M: SiO excitation poorly constrained; more SiO lines needed
- 2019PASJ...71...68K: Nucleus distance is hard to determine due to line of sight
- 2019PASJ...71...68K: CO(3-2) shows negative signals from sparse uv coverage
- 2018ApJ...864..133T: Beam smear not corrected, affecting inner 90-100 au
- 2018ApJ...864..133T: Neighbouring annuli are correlated within a beam
- 2015ApJ...813..128Q: Data give no N2H+ constraints beyond a few hundred AU; C18O fit imperfect in inner disk
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Dust masses and dust-to-gas ratios uncertain by about a factor of 5
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Extended emission may be resolved out
- 2016MNRAS.460.2933M: Dust mass depends strongly on assumed composition and amax; h not fully constrained
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: Missing flux on large scales biases rotation velocities at large radii
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: SO is optically thick so density and abundance unconstrained
- 2019ApJ...873...50D: Parameterized Sérsic modeling cannot independently constrain faint emission at large radii
- 2019ApJ...873...50D: Simple Sérsic profiles unlikely to fully characterize source structure
- 2017ApJ...837...93Y: Orbit not determined a priori; line-of-sight velocity and position unknown
- 2024A&A...689A..64B: CS results poorly constrained, source size fixed at 1.6"
- 2024A&A...689A..64B: Comparing GMC-scale NGC 253 with parsec scale Galactic regions
- 2020ApJ...897L..33J: Some centroid positional errors are large at high velocities; RRL masers are variable
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: alpha_CO very uncertain and held constant
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: Missing flux for some lines
- 2020MNRAS.492.1180R: Resolution too low to resolve cavity wall layers; speculative conclusions
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Model not formally fit; chosen by eye
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Mass-loss rate is a lower limit as optical depth is about unity
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: LVG parameters highly degenerate; best-fit values reflect relative trends only
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: Sample biased to upper main sequence and warm dust by PACS detection requirement
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Total belt flux is model-dependent due to extrapolation to zero uv distance; position angle and inclination unconstrained
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Low target elevation and antenna shadowing
- 2024ApJ...966..117X: Single 60 Msun core evolutionary sequence; PDR effects ignored; fitted masses not reliable
- 2013ApJ...778L..25C: Emitting region unresolved; higher resolution and 2D/3D modeling needed
- 2020ApJ...898...61I: Absolute Sigma_mol depends critically on alpha_CO, and inclination is unknown
- 2020ApJ...898...61I: Modest S/N prevents line profile/outflow analysis
- 2014A&A...566A.112M: CO and C I column densities highly uncertain in SW wings and NE
- 2024ESC.....8..665M: Coarse resolution; morphology cannot be determined
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: Dominance of H2 in the CND is assumed; HI/HII may contribute
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: RADEX assumes single homogeneous medium though real structure is complex; single transition limits Tex
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: HDO and H2O observed ~2 weeks apart; Q(H2O) inferred via CH3OH proxy
- 2025NatAs...9.1476C: Low S/N of HDO leaves L_p unconstrained for 50% distributed case
- 2025ApJ...991...53C: Halo internal structure and magnification are poorly constrained; lens redshifts uncertain
- 2019A&A...632A.101T: Outflow parameters are local/lower limits since ALMA field does not cover full outflows; inclination uncorrected; absolute forces uncertain by factors of a few
- 2019A&A...632A.101T: HCN optically thick so abundances lower limits; H2CO may be underestimated
- 2017ApJ...840....8S: alpha_CO largest uncertainty from x_CO assumption
- 2019ApJ...882..160Q: Velocity-offset uncertainty hard to determine for low-inclination disks
- 2013ApJ...765L..14Q: Low S/N prevents constraining the vertical distribution; weak lines unresolved
- 2013ApJ...765L..14Q: 3-2 and 5-4 lines lie at the edge of the spectral window
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Spherical symmetry assumed despite asymmetric emission
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Weak lines too low S/N for uv fitting
- 2017ApJ...839...86H: Grid search does not characterize uncertainties on CO parameters
- 2013ApJ...770..142N: ALMA data lack zero-spacing; HDO collision rates only up to 450 K so highest HDO lines cannot be modeled; vibrational pumping excluded
- 2019A&A...628A..23A: LVG model not fully constrained because the CO SLED peak is not traced
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: Distance mismatch between GRS 1915+105 and IRAS source; jet power assumes constant power and density
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: ALMA continuum lacks single-dish data so flux is underestimated
- 2024A&A...686A..47M: Only two measurements for r51 and r71; single-component LVG inadequate
- 2020ApJ...895..119T: ACA missing flux; limited resolution cannot resolve protoplanetary disk; velocity difference near spectral resolution
- 2015ApJ...801...63M: Error maps too optimistic; negative bowl from missing short spacings; region 6 fluxes highly uncertain due to absorption
- 2020A&A...637A...7M: Non-simultaneous XD and XH observations and time variability; high uncertainties
- 2020A&A...637A...7M: Assumed covering factor of 1
- 2021A&A...655A..80D: 1D model cannot account for 3D asymmetry; true uncertainties much larger than formal ones
- 2020ApJ...902..109B: PDR results only qualitative; small sample; selection effects cannot be fully excluded
- 2020MNRAS.497.2811K: Dust masses have large systematic uncertainties from arbitrary composition; HD 129590 gas unconstrained by MCMC
- 2024MNRAS.529.3601R: Velocity resolution inadequate to constrain kinematics
- 2015MNRAS.453.4324M: Predicted fluxes are only order-of-magnitude estimates
- 2020ApJ...892L..18I: Core component interpretation not conclusive.
- 2015ApJ...808...97Y: SFR is only an order of magnitude estimate
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Rgd for diffuse Milky Way gas may not apply to the dense CMZ
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: H3O+/SO ratio affected by optical depth and calibration; factor of two differences possible
- 2019ApJ...871..170M: Total Power data unusable so no zero-spacing beyond ACA
- 2019ApJ...880...69Y: Spiral velocities depend on the assumed mid-plane location and conserved angular momentum
- 2019ApJ...880...69Y: Inner-radius line width overestimated, so column density, Tex and tau at the inner radius may be underestimated
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Models are degenerate, not unique or optimal; systematic residuals at large radii
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Band 7 sky frequency in SV measurement set incorrect
- 2017A&A...597A..27S: Severe flux loss, no short-spacing data; ~30% recovered near systemic velocity, so structures there are excluded
- 2017A&A...597A..27S: Geometry uncertainties are not quantified; fit is only fair
- 2019AJ....157..117M: Inner hole not resolved with this dataset
- 2019AJ....157..117M: Single CO transition leaves excitation unconstrained; mass uncertain over two orders of magnitude
- 2013ApJ...773L..34K: Collision rates unknown; LTE SLEDs for J>3-2 are upper limits; SPIRE limits cannot constrain model
- 2017ApJ...845..154V: Molecular gas uncertainties exclude CO SLED shape uncertainty; low-J CO needed

