### 2019PASJ...71...68K: A Chandra and ALMA study of X-ray-irradiated gas in the central ∼100 pc of the Circinus galaxy (2019; nearby_galaxies, agn_and_quasars; archival_reuse)
- question: Does AGN X-ray irradiation dissociate molecular gas in the central ~100 pc of Circinus, as seen by comparing the Chandra Fe Kα map with ALMA dense-gas lines?
- step 7: Constrain gas physical conditions with non-LTE modelling
  - method: RADEX grid over Tkin 10-600 K, log nH2 2-7, log NH2 20-25, [HCN]/[HCO+] 1-10; chi-square fit to 10 line ratios [5.1.2 RADEX Non-LTE Modeling: "We simulate 10 combinations of line ratios taken from the five lines for various kinetic temperatures ($T_{\rm kin}$), hydrogen densities ($n_{\rm H2}$), and hydrogen column densities ($N_{\rm mol}$)."]
  - software: RADEX, LAMDA
  - parameter: Line widths fixed at average 3 sigma width: 330, 120, 140 km/s for Nucleus, CNR-E, CNR-SE [5.1.2 RADEX Non-LTE Modeling: "330 km s$^{-1}$, 120 km s$^{-1}$, and 140 km s$^{-1}$ for the Nucleus, CNR-E and CNR-SE regions, respectively"]
  - assumption: Spherical homogeneous geometry; Tbg = 2.73 K; [CO]/[H2]=6e-5, [HCO+]/[H2]=8e-9 [5.1.2 RADEX Non-LTE Modeling: "A spherically, homogeneous geometry is assumed in the code."]
  - fitting: Chi-square grid [5.1.2 RADEX Non-LTE Modeling: "These parameters are constrained by the chi-square method."]
  - validation: Alternative abundances tested; conclusion not strongly affected [5.1.2 RADEX Non-LTE Modeling: "our conclusion in Section [6.3](#sec:xdr) is not strongly affected"]
- step 8: Compute XDR effective ionization parameter
  - method: xi_eff ≈ 0.1 L_X,44 / (n_H2,4 R_100^2 N_H,22^alpha) using RADEX densities, 60-62 pc distances, log NH = 23.9 [6.3 XDR Model: "The distances from the center to the CNR-E and CNR-SE regions were set to 62 pc and 60 pc, respectively."]
  - parameter: L(1-100 keV)=1.3e43 erg/s, Gamma 2.31, alpha ≈1.1 [6.3 XDR Model: "The photon index corresponds to $\alpha \approx$1.1."]
  - assumption: Nucleus distance R > 60 pc; gas-phase C and O abundances 3e-4 and 5e-4 [6.3 XDR Model: "The gas-phase abundance of C and O with respect to H is assumed to be $3.0\times10^{-4}$ and $5.0\times10^{-4}$, respectively."]
  - validation: Repeated with luminosities from INTEGRAL, BeppoSAX, Suzaku; same conclusion [6.3 XDR Model: "In either case, low ionization parameters of $\log \xi_{\rm eff} \approx -3$ are derived, however."]
- result: RADEX log n(H2), CNR-E = 3.5 ± +1.5/-0.5 log cm^-3 [Table 6: "CNR-E& 24.5$^{+0.5}_{-4.5}$ & 3.5$^{+1.5}_{-0.5}$ & 200$^{+130}_{-150}$"]
- result: RADEX log n(H2), CNR-SE = 4.5 ± +0.0/-1.5 log cm^-3 [Table 6: "CNR-SE& 23.5$^{+1.5}_{-0.0}$ & 4.5$^{+0.0}_{-1.5}$ & 130$^{+270}_{-50}$"]
- result: RADEX log n(H2), Nucleus = 5.0 ± +0.0/-0.5 log cm^-3 [Table 6: "Nucleus & 24.5$^{+0.5}_{-0.0}$ & 5.0$^{+0.0}_{-0.5}$ & 290$^{+110}_{-100}$"]
- result: log xi_eff CNR-E = -4.6 to -2.6 ± range dimensionless [6.3 XDR Model: "the ionization parameters in the CNR-E and CNR-SE regions are $\log \xi_{\rm eff} = -4.6\sim-2.6$ and $-4.0\sim-2.5$, respectively."]
- result: log xi_eff Nucleus = < -4.0 ± upper limit dimensionless [6.3 XDR Model: "The low ionization parameter of $\log \xi_{\rm eff} < -4.0$ in the Nucleus"]
- limitation (authors): Nucleus distance is hard to determine due to line of sight [6.3 XDR Model: "The distance appropriate for the Nucleus region is difficult to determine due to the sightline."]
- limitation (authors): CO(3-2) shows negative signals from sparse uv coverage [5.1 Reduction and Reprocessing of ALMA …: "some negative signals were found around the line, likely due to the high brightness and sparse $uv$-coverage."]
